{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1378122-statting-gerlat-of-rivia-witcher-as-a-starting-dawn","id":1378122,"title":"Statting Gerlat of Rivia (Witcher) as a starting dawn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-02T17:59:11-07:00","id":1378122,"title":"Statting Gerlat of Rivia (Witcher) as a starting dawn","content":"Hi All.<br /> Trying to stat a dawn solar that's inspired by Geralt.<br /> His supernal would be melee? (or maybe resistance, he gets knocked about quite a lot and always manages to recover)<br /> In terms of attributes: primary is obviously physical, secondary mental and tertiary social.<br /> STR: 3 CHR: 3 PER:4<br /> DEX: 4 MAN: 1* INT:2<br /> STA: 4 APP: 3 WIT:3<br /> * geralt is blunt, not much of a manipulator <br /> <br /> Caste skills: Melee 5,Resistance 3,awareness 3, brawl 2, throw 1<br /> Favorite skills: Investigation 4, Presence 4, Occult 3, Integrity 2, <br /> for the last one i'm torn between athletics and survival (to track monsters)<br /> General skills: lore 1, linguistics 1, the other skill (athletics or survival)<br /> <br /> Does this seem right?<br /> Which charms would you choose?<br /> <br /> Adi<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4939-adimar","name":"adimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T01:35:26-07:00","id":1378206,"title":"","content":"Sounds good enough.<br /> I'd invest more heavily in resistance, but his recovery can be emulated mostly through one charm already.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would also cap awareness earlier, and get the keen senses early too.<br /> <br /> Signs don't translate well to anything canon, but you should find reasonable homebrew, this topic comes and goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T07:06:21-07:00","id":1378258,"title":"","content":"To be clear, we're talking a Dawn inspired by The Witcher?<br /> <br /> Looks great.<br /> <br /> You have built a character in line with the expectations of the game. I would take Survival.<br /> <br /> I would spend bonus points on (your caste/favoured abilities in order to buy) Athletics and Dodge up to 2.<br /> <br /> Charms, I suggest ignoring Geralt's signs and going for:<br /> <br /> Melee<br /> 1. Excellent Strike<br /> 2. Dipping Swallow Defence<br /> 3. Fire and Stones Strike<br /> 4. Bulwark Stance<br /> 5. Five Fold Bulwark Stance<br /> 6. Hail Shattering Practice<br /> <br /> Resistance<br /> <br /> 7. Ox-Body Technique<br /> 8. Ox-Body Technique \u00d72<br /> 9. Body-Mending Meditation<br /> <br /> Occult<br /> 10. Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> --Shaping Ritual: Soul-Pefecting Elixer<br /> --Control Spell: Invulnerable Skin of Deathly Grey Pallor (Invulnerable Skin of Bronze)<br /> <br /> Presence<br /> 11. Listener Swaying Argument<br /> 12. Tiger's Dread Symmetry<br /> <br /> Athletics<br /> 13. Graceful Crane Stance<br /> <br /> Dodge<br /> 14. Reed in the Wind<br /> <br /> Brawl<br /> 15. Thunderclap Rush Technique<br /> <br /> This is by no means &quot;optimal&quot;. If you optimize you are likely to leave your character concept in the dust. This is meant to be a fun &quot;inspired by&quot; build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T07:07:04-07:00","id":1378259,"title":"","content":"He should have craft water, for all the potions and brewing he does.<br /> <br /> And he uses a crossbow a lot in Witcher 3. So definitely put in some archery.<br /> <br /> He rides Roach a lot. So put in some ride too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3012,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","user":"Uknown DarkLord","date":". 04-03-2020, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T07:59:01-07:00","id":1378268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1378122-statting-gerlat-of-rivia-witcher-as-a-starting-dawn?p=1378259#post1378259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He should have craft water, for all the potions and brewing he does.<br /> <br /> And he uses a crossbow a lot in Witcher 3. So definitely put in some archery.<br /> <br /> He rides Roach a lot. So put in some ride too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Craft Water doesn't exist. But yeah, Craft Potions is pretty key.<br /> <br /> Archery you could take or leave.<br /> <br /> He never fights on the back of Roach. I wouldn't sweat the Ride dots. Challenging riding for heroes will be difficulty 1, and Gerald is throwing six dice at that with a Stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}